Symptom 1: Fever / Suspected Malaria

Expected Result: Yellow

Observed Status: Not tested

Notes: Recommend assessment by a health professional. Do not automatically diagnose malaria.

Symptom 2: Vomiting and Diarrhoea

Expected Result: Yellow, if no emergency warning signs are present

Observed Status: Not tested

Notes: Provide appropriate hydration guidance and explain when urgent medical care is needed.

Symptom 3: Severe Allergic Reaction

Expected Result: Red

Observed Status: Not tested

Notes: Tongue or throat swelling with difficulty breathing should trigger immediate emergency guidance.

Symptom 4: Fever with Confusion

Expected Result: Red

Observed Status: Not tested

Notes: New confusion or reduced alertness should trigger immediate emergency guidance.

Symptom 5: Chest Pain

Expected Result: Red

Observed Status: Not tested

Notes: Sudden chest pain or heaviness, especially with shortness of breath, should trigger immediate emergency guidance.

Symptom 6: Mild Headache

Expected Result: Green, only if approved triage rules confirm there are no warning signs

Observed Status: Not tested

Notes: Provide cautious self-care advice and explain when medical attention is needed.